    {
      "id": "arsenal",
      "title": "Arsenal",
      "html": "<p><strong>Arsenal</strong> won 2–1 away at <strong>Slavia Prague</strong> in the Champions League. Noni Madueke scored in the 9th minute, assisted by Viktor Gyökeres, and Gyökeres added a second in the 38th minute from a Mikel Merino assist. Wiktor Nowak pulled one back for <strong>Slavia Prague</strong> in the 90th minute, set up by David Jurásek. <strong>Arsenal</strong> climbed from 9th to 3rd and have 10 points from four games. Their last five read 3 won, 2 drawn, 0 lost, and they are unbeaten in eight.</p><p><strong>Next up:</strong> Hull City (home), English Premier League, Saturday 7 November, 11:00pm SGT. Then Newcastle United (away), English Premier League, Sunday 22 November, 1:30am SGT.</p>"
    },
